ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":122,"prev":124,"next":127,"titles":129,"firmware":29},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":13,"order":14,"path":15,"context":16,"summary":22,"status":23,"firmware":24,"facts":30,"procedures":66,"parameters":74,"related":102,"body":106,"sources":107,"official_url":34,"controls":116},"sequencer.bar-menu","Bar menu",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],"bar page","bar screen","quantise","quantize","quantisation","note length","track groove","lock smoothing","sequencer",60,"knowledge/manual/units/sequencer/bar-menu.md",{"modes":17,"screens":20},[18,19],"instrument","auxiliary",[21],"bar","Holding `bar` shows the selected track's pattern settings; the encoders set quantisation, note length, groove and lock smoothing, and other keys handle bars, track scale, length and clearing.","current",{"min":25,"changed_in":26,"guide_version":27,"verified_on":29},"1.0.9",[27,28],"1.1.15","1.1.25","1.1.33",[31,37,42,46,49,54,57,60,63],{"id":32,"text":33,"source":34,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":35,"confidence":36},"held","The bar page stays on screen only while `bar` is held; `shift + bar` pins it until you press `bar` again.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sequencer#extend-with-bar",null,"official",{"id":38,"text":39,"source":40,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":29,"confidence":41},"quantise-default","In a new project the card reads quant 100, length 50 and track scale 1, with groove shown as a dash and shape as a small step symbol.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#28-bar-steps","verified",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":45,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":35,"confidence":36},"odd-grid","Since OS 1.1.25, tracks with an odd track scale (3, 5, 6 or 7) quantise to a grid made for that scale.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.25",{"id":47,"text":48,"source":34,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":35,"confidence":36},"groove-type","The groove type (shuffle, bombora and the rest) is picked on the tempo page; the bar menu sets only this track's amount.",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":52,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":35,"confidence":53},"per-pattern","Decoded project files store length, track scale, quantisation, groove and smoothing in each pattern, so a track's patterns can differ.","docs/research/10-xy-format.md#34-patternstruct-base-clones-walking","community-verified",{"id":55,"text":56,"source":40,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":29,"confidence":41},"card","Holding `bar` lays a white card over the dimmed page — bar numbers 1 to 4 along the top with the current one inverted, the track scale beside them, then rows for quant, length, groove and shape, each marked with its encoder's dot. The card fades when `bar` is let go.",{"id":58,"text":59,"source":40,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":29,"confidence":41},"roll","A faint mini piano roll on the right of the card shows a dash for each note in the shown bar, as long as the note.",{"id":61,"text":62,"source":40,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":29,"confidence":41},"boxes-live","With the card up, `bar + [+]` or `bar + [-]` adds or removes a bar box at once; the shown bar's box is filled and the other bars are outlined.",{"id":64,"text":65,"source":40,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":29,"confidence":41},"clear-labels","The card's footer names the clearing keys — clr notes on `M1`, clr params on `M2`, clr all on `M4`.",[67],{"id":68,"goal":69,"preconditions":70,"steps":71,"result":35,"source":34,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":35,"confidence":36},"adjust","Change a pattern-wide setting",[],[72],{"keys":73,"note":35,"set":35},"bar + turn E1…E4",[75,80,87,91,96],{"screen":21,"encoder":76,"layer":77,"keys":78,"name":9,"range":35,"default":35,"cc":35,"cc_confidence":35,"note":79,"source":34,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":35,"confidence":36},"E1","base","turn E1","pulls live-recorded notes onto the steps; at 100 nothing can be nudged",{"screen":21,"encoder":76,"layer":81,"keys":82,"name":83,"range":35,"default":35,"cc":35,"cc_confidence":35,"note":84,"source":85,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":35,"confidence":86},"click","click E1","quantisation on/off","1.1.15 added a click that toggles quantisation; that it is this encoder is assumed","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.15","derived",{"screen":21,"encoder":88,"layer":77,"keys":89,"name":10,"range":35,"default":35,"cc":35,"cc_confidence":35,"note":90,"source":34,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":35,"confidence":36},"E2","turn E2","for notes entered by pressing steps",{"screen":21,"encoder":92,"layer":77,"keys":93,"name":94,"range":35,"default":35,"cc":35,"cc_confidence":35,"note":95,"source":34,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":35,"confidence":36},"E3","turn E3","groove","this track's amount; replaces the tempo page's swing",{"screen":21,"encoder":97,"layer":77,"keys":98,"name":99,"range":35,"default":100,"cc":35,"cc_confidence":35,"note":101,"source":34,"firmware_min":35,"verified_on":35,"confidence":36},"E4","turn E4","shape","no smoothing","smooths between parameter locks and recorded automation",[103,104,105],"sequencer.track-scale","sequencer.bars-and-length","sequencer.clear-and-undo","Everything here acts on the whole pattern, whereas step edits and locks act on single steps. The\nkeys handle structure — `[+]` and `[-]` add and remove bars, black keys set the track scale, step\nkeys set the length, `M1`, `M2` and `M4` clear — while the encoders handle feel.",[108,110,112,114,115],{"url":34,"kind":109},"guide",{"url":40,"kind":111},"research",{"url":45,"kind":113},"changelog",{"url":52,"kind":111},{"url":85,"kind":113},[117,118,119,120,121],"key.bar","encoder.1","encoder.2","encoder.3","encoder.4",{"id":13,"title":123},"Sequencer",{"id":125,"title":126},"sequencer.component-skip-trigger","Skip trigger (step component)",{"id":103,"title":128},"Track scale",{"basics.key-notation":130,"basics.main-modes":131,"basics.modules":132,"basics.track-buttons":133,"basics.linked-tracks":134,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":135,"basics.workflow":136,"basics.firmware-versions":137